<title>USA: Sprint to cut weekend intl rates - paper.</title>
<headline>Sprint to cut weekend intl rates - paper.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sprint Corp will announce on Monday it is cutting international weekend telephone rates to as low as $0.10 per minute, USA Today said.</p>
<p>Weekend calls to Germany, Italy and France would be about $0.30 per minute, down from $0.45 per minute, and calls to India would be $1.05 per minute, down from $1.15 per minute, the newspaper said on Monday.</p>
<p>Weekend calls to England would be nearly as cheap as a domestic call, the newspaper said.</p>
<p>Weekday rates are higher, USA Today said.</p>
<p>((New York newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
